    "C3 (inviolable): the three final queries that expect absence are answered absent.",
    "C4 (inviolable, the semantic requirement): at least three of the six final requests in Italian are correct; a lexical configuration is not exempt.",
    "C5 (inviolable): at least ten of the twenty final queries are correct (coverage, selection, exclusions, bindings, conditions and alternatives all as expected).",
    "C6 (measured, not a criterion of correctness): warm search p95 on the corpus within 50 ms on the release build; the load, memory and scale budgets are checkpoint 5's.",
    "Choice: among the configurations that meet C1 to C5, fewest unsafe answers, then most correct, then the simpler channel (lexical, semantic, hybrid), then the smaller lexical weight, then the name. If none meets them the failure is reported, no configuration is declared validated, and the product keeps a provisional configuration said as such."
